The Day 256 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. It is not committed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so the requested git commit … || true does nothing. At first I force-added it, then undid that commit, and the file stays on disk for the planner. HEAD is still e9966f43.

What I found by running the built binary (fake home folder, no real server contacted):
• #1177 reaches a real run, not just the parser. With model = "m1" # c in .yoyo.toml, both yoyo config get model and the run's opening line say the model is "m1" # c. So the quotes and the comment are sent as the model id. Python's TOML reader (tomllib) reads that line as m1. I didn't re-run the other half: the ticket's earlier test showed that deny = ["/tmp"] # x comes back as an empty list, so the blocked-folders list silently isn't applied and nothing warns.
• Retired GitHub Models is still offered (#1166, not finished): --provider nosuch lists github among the known providers.
• Two files are close to the size limit. src/context.rs is 2035 lines and not in the size-limit exception list. 15 more lines would make cargo test fail, which reverts the whole task. src/help.rs is 10 lines from the same failure.

Recent runs: the last 4 evolve runs succeeded and the current one is in progress. The one CI failure in the window (2026-11-10) came from a clock-timing flaky test, fixed in the Day 255 12:08 session. No reverts in 14 days.

Research:
• How Codex handles its config file: it uses a real TOML parser. Config errors show the file, line and column, with the bad text underlined, and the program exits with an error. Unknown keys are accepted by default, with an opt-in strict mode. yoyo reads its config line by line by hand and has no TOML library at all. That's why the last three config tickets (#1171, #1174, #1177) each found one more format it misreads. I saved this comparison to yopedia.
• Claude Code's changelog (Nov 3–10): it now warns when both an auth token and an API key are set. I haven't checked whether yoyo has the same gap.

Suggested order for the planner:
1. #1177, done the way the ticket now asks: one shared comment-stripping helper for every config value reader, plus a test that compares yoyo with tomllib over a set of TOML examples. Formats yoyo can't read should be refused with a warning, not misread. Switching to a real TOML library would need a decision from @yuanhao about adding a dependency.
2. #1175: the custom provider defaults to an Anthropic model id even though the user runs their own server.
3. #1166: take github out of the known-providers list.
4. Register or split src/context.rs before any task touches it.
